# Noorix Delivery Batching Policy

This rule has higher priority than automatic publish habits.

## Default Execution Rule

Work in large, scoped batches. Do not split related safe work into many small PRs.

Each batch must have:

| Item | Required |
|---|---|
| Scope | one clear phase, not scattered opportunistic fixes |
| Definition of done | explicit before implementation |
| Verification | commands matched to the change |
| Risk boundary | protected financial/tax/payroll/bank/print areas identified |
| Delivery | one PR for the batch, one merge, one live deploy only when needed |

## PR and Deploy Rules

| Case | Action |
|---|---|
| Runtime or production behavior changed | PR, CI, merge, deploy, live verification |
| Docs/governance only | do not deploy by itself; bundle with the next large batch unless explicitly requested |
| Small typo or isolated note | keep local or bundle; no standalone PR unless blocking CI |
| Emergency production fix | small PR allowed |
| User explicitly asks to publish now | publish after verification |

## Forbidden Pattern

Do not do this:

```txt
small edit -> PR -> CI -> merge -> deploy
small doc -> PR -> CI -> merge -> deploy
small governance tweak -> PR -> CI -> merge -> deploy
```

Use this instead:

```txt
plan phase -> implement complete batch -> run relevant checks -> one PR -> CI -> merge -> one deploy if runtime changed
```

## Stop Condition

When a phase is closed, do not open a new adjacent improvement automatically. Report:

- what is complete
- what remains
- whether the next item is a new phase
- whether it should wait for user approval

